From 9e145e212c931ea4d7b3ee1f457d80b54675796e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:14:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Guardian G18: bound DoT connect time; emulator DoT step
 checks reachability

Run 41646471550 (feature/G18b) and 41644698809 failed at emulator step
4g: with Quad9 chosen a lookup got no answer for over 30 s. DotClient
could spend addresses x connect timeout per attempt and then sweep all
addresses again: about 32 s against a provider whose packets are
dropped, far past the system resolver's patience.

DotClient: connect timeout 3 s, a 5 s total connect budget per query,
and the retry only for a reused connection the resolver had closed, not
after a fresh connect already failed. DotClientTest +2 (blackholed
provider gives up within the budget with at most 3 attempts; a closed
reused connection is retried once). Mutations (no budget, re-sweep
after a fresh failure) each fail the new test.

Emulator flow: resolve() treats an adb timeout as "no answer" instead
of crashing the flow; step 4g first checks from the CI host that
Quad9:853 accepts TCP (address read from DotProviders.kt) and prints
UNTESTED and skips if not; on failure it prints the encrypted DNS
status line so the cause is visible.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
